ob/three.js/pulls/6769","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/6769","diff_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/6769.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/pull/6769.patch","merged_at":"2015-07-02T10:02:07Z"},"body":"Fixes #5813.\n\nThe infinite loop needs to be converted to a finite loop. I arbitrarily chose 30 as the max number of iterations for the loop to break on its own - it's not very large but experimentally, it seems to be enough.\n\nI initially tried larger numbers, but they were causing trouble:\n- The bigger the number, the slowest the shader. It takes approximately ~2 seconds for IE11 to compile the shader with `i < 250`.\n- For any termination value above `277`, IE11 will simply not render...\n\nFor reference, Chrome and Firefox had no problem with very large termination condition.\n\nThe new loop header also fixes a warning in Chrome / ANGLE.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/6769/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/6769/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/comments/118026673","html_url":"https://github.com/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5813#issuecomment-118026673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mrdoob/three.js/issues/5813","id":118026673,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExODAyNjY3Mw==","user":{"login":"dubejf","id":8649151,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2NDkxNTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8649151?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dubejf","html_url":"https://github.com/dubejf","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dubejf/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dubejf/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dubejf/gists{/gist_id}"